//  The leap branch is replaced by an alt fire. Same slot in the dynamic: it is
//  tried before the normal whip attack, and falls through to it whenever the
//  cooldown, the chance roll, the ability check or the range check says no.
//
//  nicemice_resolveAbilityIntent gates it. On a two-handed whip the alt SLOT is
//  unusable -- the engine routes alt fire to the primary item's altAbility -- so
//  this reads nicemice_gentlereminder's altAbilityType (energyorb). It also
//  fails cleanly if a whip has no alt ability or it is flagged npcDoNotUse.
//
//  energyorb is an instant ability: it throws a gravityless projectile the
//  moment it activates. So altFireTime is a trigger, not a charge hold -- long
//  enough to register one activation and then release. Lengthening it re-fires
//  the ability rather than charging it. (Staves are the opposite: they need a
//  hold past the charge stance and then a release, which is what
//  nicemice_chargedFire and the wandstaff tree's three phases are for.)
//
//  The projectile has no gravity, so aiming straight at the target is correct
//  and no arc solution is needed -- but it does travel in a line, hence the
//  entityInSight gate.
//
//    altFireCooldown  seconds between alt casts
//    altFireChance    roll each time the cooldown is up
//    altFireRange     radial range gate, and the fallback cast range
//    altFireTime      how long alt fire is held; one activation, then release
